"Avowed can make voice calls, video calls on a floating circular screen, texts and group calls."
"Contact priorities control who can text an Avowed."
"A System call from Artona III to Earth costs a few thousand dollars."
"Mental commands on the System take practice to master."
"Cross-dimensional contact costs 500 Argold to connect plus 3 Argold a minute, in any medium."
"Local calls are cheap."
"Granting contact permission lets someone call you at their own expense."
"A low-priority contact is put in a queue."
"The System can send a selfie, and video callers can appear as a floating face."
"The System stops translating official magic lessons, and callers may authorize translation."
"Lockers on Artona III alert their owner through the System if anyone opens them."
"Messages stored on Earth can be sent across in one packet for a standard connection fee."
"Calls from high-ranking callers do not auto-connect, and their connection fee may be waived."
"Incoming calls are color-coded; strangers show in subtle brown."
"Calls to far worlds like Sreeeakk cost extreme magical long-distance rates."
"Superhumans keep a well-honored rule against System spam; ads come on paper."
"Avowed can show optional interface name tags with personal details."
"Every Avowed's brain is wired into the planet's magical communications array."
"Calls are accepted with a thought, and a caller can zoom out to see the callee's surroundings."
"Mental texting can garble, or reach the wrong person when juggling people and languages."
"Interfaces can block messages from non-friends or recently renamed senders."
